<!--
  The hand-off between a session and its deliveries on the cooperative engine (wz-capi-coop
  `lane::SharedLane`): two queues of this document, one carrying each sample the session
  published to the deliveries, one carrying it back once its callbacks have returned.

  One producer and one consumer, which the engine has without serialising anything itself:
    - the producer of the forward queue and the consumer of the return queue is whoever holds the
      session's lock, under which every sample is written (the read step, a put of the session's
      own, a declaration handed the tokens already known), so one holder at a time;
    - the consumer of the forward queue and the producer of the return queue is whoever holds the
      lane's delivery word, taken by a compare-exchange, so one delivery at a time; a delivery
      that finds it held leaves the samples to the holder, which looks again as it lets go.

  wait-free: the selection table gives one producer and one consumer the Lamport ring, a load and
  a store of an index on each side. The producer publishes an element with a Release store of its
  index and the consumer reads the index with Acquire before the element, so the sample's record
  and bytes, written before the push, are seen by the delivery that pops it; the return queue
  orders the end of the callbacks before the session reuses the slot the same way.

  Capacity 64 is the build's DELIVERY_LANE_EVENTS (the lane's event slots,
  WZ_LIMIT_DELIVERY_LANE_EVENTS): a queue holds at most a handle per slot the lane has out, so it
  never refuses one. The consumer asserts at compile time that the capacity is at least the build's
  limit, so a build that raises the limit is told to raise this number with it.
-->
<scxml xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/07/scxml"
       xmlns:sce="http://sce.dev/ext"
       sce:kind="queue"
       name="delivery_lane_queue"
       version="1.0">
  <sce:element-type>delivery_lane_handle</sce:element-type>
  <sce:producers>one</sce:producers>
  <sce:consumers>one</sce:consumers>
  <sce:progress>wait-free</sce:progress>
  <sce:bounded capacity="64"/>
</scxml>
